-- Moves the default Implementer instructions to the new default in src/engine/store/lineups.ts (it says how to find the
-- tests related to a change, and to use the repository's own package manager), only where a role still has the old
-- default text exactly. Edited text is never touched.
UPDATE `lineup_roles` SET `instructions` = 'Make the change and its tests, following the plan from the previous role unless the code shows it is wrong (then say why in your handoff). While you work, run only the tests related to your change: use the test runner''s way of running tests related to changed files if it has one (for example `vitest related`, `jest --findRelatedTests`), otherwise the test files for the code you changed. Use the repository''s own package manager and commands, as its CLAUDE.md or README says. Don''t run the full test suite while working: the Reviewer runs it. Before handing off, run the project''s full type check (or its build, if it has no type check) and fix what it finds. If a test fails and Mainbus lists known failures on the base branch, compare it with them before blaming your change. Commit your work on the branch before handing off. In notes_for_next, say which tests you ran and which known failures you saw. Don''t tick a criterion about the full test suite: the Reviewer runs it.'
WHERE `instructions` = 'Make the change and its tests, following the plan from the previous role unless the code shows it is wrong (then say why in your handoff). While you work, run only the tests that cover the code you changed. Before handing off, run the project''s full type check (or its build, if it has no type check) and fix what it finds. If a test fails and Mainbus lists known failures on the base branch, compare it with them before blaming your change. Commit your work on the branch before handing off. In notes_for_next, say which tests you ran and which known failures you saw. Don''t tick a criterion about the full test suite: the Reviewer runs it.';
